my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
one
two
three
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{Ctrl-r redoes the last undone change},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/redo_ctrl_r`

Tests that **Ctrl-r** redoes the most recently undone change.
The flow is: delete a line, undo it, then redo it.

**Keys:** `dd`, `u`, `Control-r`

**initial.png**
- Buffer has 3 lines: "one", "two", "three"
- Cursor on line 1

**after_dd.png**
- Buffer has 2 lines: "two", "three"
- "one" deleted
- Intermediate snapshot after deletion

**after_undo.png**
- Buffer restored to 3 lines (identical to initial)
- "one" restored by undo
- Intermediate snapshot after undo

**after_redo.png**
- Buffer back to 2 lines: "two", "three"
- "one" deleted again by redo
- Same state as after_dd
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('dd');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_dd');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('u');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_undo');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('Control-r');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_redo');
    },
}
